class:: SemiMarkov
summary:: Finite-state process with state-specific dwell distributions
categories:: UGens>Control>Markov
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/MarkovChain, Classes/RenewalTrig

description::

Combines a Markov transition matrix with a dwell-time distribution for each state. The duration Buffer has three channels: mean seconds, shape, and code (0 fixed, 1 exponential, 2 gamma, 3 Weibull, 4 lognormal).

At most one transition occurs per calculation and negative timing remainder is carried. Like link::Classes/MarkovChain::, it selects state from row-major weights; unlike MarkovChain, time rather than an external trigger schedules transitions.

subsection:: State and dwell view

image::semi-markov-dynamics.png#Left: a three-state semi-Markov realization using fixed, gamma, and Weibull dwell laws. Right: remaining dwell time counting down and resampling at transitions; the varying ramp heights make timing part of the model state.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: numStates
Init-rate state count, clipped to 1 through 256.
argument:: transitionBuf
One-channel row-major code::numStates*numStates:: weights.
argument:: durationBuf
Three-channel Buffer with code::numStates:: frames: mean, shape, distribution code.
argument:: valueBuf
Optional one-channel values; negative uses state index.
argument:: initialState
Rounded and clipped initial state.
argument:: timeScale
Nonnegative countdown speed. Zero pauses.
argument:: seed
Init-rate local seed.
argument:: reset
Restore state and seed and schedule its first duration.
returns:: State, mapped value, one-calculation changed trigger, remaining seconds.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments and outputs.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
Routine {
    b = Buffer.loadCollection(s, [0.8, 0.2, 0.3, 0.7]);
    c = Buffer.loadCollection(s, [1, 1, 0, 0.2, 1, 1], 3);
    s.sync;
    x = { SemiMarkov.kr(2, b, c)[0].poll }.play;
}.play;
)
::

code::
(
Routine {
    b = Buffer.loadCollection(s, [
        0.7, 0.2, 0.1,
        0.2, 0.6, 0.2,
        0.1, 0.3, 0.6
    ]);
    c = Buffer.loadCollection(s, [
        0.6, 1, 0,
        0.2, 2, 2,
        1.4, 0.5, 3
    ], 3);
    d = Buffer.loadCollection(s, [180, 420, 900]);
    s.sync;
    x = {
        var process = SemiMarkov.kr(3, b, c, d);
        SinOsc.ar(process[1], 0, Decay2.kr(process[2], 0.01, 0.2) * 0.1)
    }.play;
}.play;
)
::

